# Docker never reads .gitignore: a file that `git` leaves alone is still shipped
# into the build context by `COPY . .` unless it is named here. Everything below
# is local scratch, build output, or a secret.
#
# Matching rules matter here (moby/patternmatcher): a pattern with no slash and
# no wildcard, like `node_modules`, is an exact match against the whole path, so
# it only covers the repo root. Use `**/name` for "at any depth".

# --- Version control and editor state -----------------------------------
.git
.github
.idea
.vscode

# --- Build output and runtime state ------------------------------------
# `server` and `trajecta` are the local `task build:go` binaries (43 MB and
# 11 MB), data/logs are runtime state, the sqlite files are legacy local indexes.
server
trajecta
tmp
dist
data
docker-data
logs
**/trace_index.sqlite3
**/*.sqlite3
**/*.sqlite3-shm
**/*.sqlite3-wal

# --- Local secrets ------------------------------------------------------
# .env is gitignored, but `COPY . .` would still copy it into the builder layer.
**/.env
**/.env.*

# --- Local scratch: DSH harness caches ---------------------------------
# .dsh-cache is ~8 GB of Go build/module caches and captured command logs,
# .dsh-bin holds prebuilt binaries and helper scripts, .gocache-dsh is the
# harness GOCACHE (~2.2 GB and 13k files that change on every tool invocation)
# and .golangci-cache-dsh its lint cache. None is an input to the image, yet
# `COPY . .` shipped them anyway: the build context was 2.32 GB, and because the
# Go cache is rewritten continuously the `COPY . .` layer hash changed on every
# build, re-running `go build` from scratch each time. The trailing globs are
# deliberate, so a future harness cache directory cannot leak back in.
.dsh-cache
.dsh-bin
.gocache*
.golangci-cache*
*-dsh

# --- Agent, worktree, and test scratch ---------------------------------
.codex
worktrees
.cache
.integration-logs
.playwright-cli
.playwright
.venv-atif
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/*.tgz

# --- Node and UI build artifacts ---------------------------------------
**/node_modules
web/monitor-ui/test-results
web/monitor-ui/playwright-report

# --- Present in the repo, but not build inputs -------------------------
# `go list -deps ./cmd/server ./cmd/trajecta` resolves every in-module
# dependency inside cmd/, internal/, pkg/ and ent/, and the only //go:embed
# targets are ent/migrations, ent/postgres-migrations and
# internal/monitor/ui/dist. The Dockerfile therefore copies exactly those four
# trees, and everything here only ever cost context bytes and hashing time. The
# Monitor frontend reaches the image as the committed internal/monitor/ui/dist;
# web/ is never built inside Docker. Remove a line if a Dockerfile step starts
# reading one of these paths.
docs
.agents
web
images
*.md
